# A write through an alias does not affect the original array

Verifies arrays keep value semantics inside a loop: rewriting the copy through
`b` leaves `a` unchanged, so the loop keeps reading `a[0]` as millimeters and
prints `11mm` on both iterations.

>>> source
let a: int[] = [10mm]
let b = a

for (i in 0..2) {
    b[0] = 2cm
    print(a[0] + 1mm)
}

<<< stdout
11mm
11mm

<<< stderr
